# 18. DIAGNOSTIC AGENT SECURITY

The local diagnostic agent is a sensitive component.

Implement strict security.

Requirements:

- Bind the service to localhost only.
- Never expose it publicly by default.
- Validate requests.
- Use an authenticated connection or secure local pairing mechanism.
- Restrict browser origins.
- Never allow arbitrary shell command execution from the web application.
- Never expose unrestricted filesystem access.
- Never upload private system information without consent.
- Clearly explain permissions.
- Provide a disconnect option.

Only implement read-only hardware inspection by default.

Any benchmark or stress test must require explicit user consent.

Do not run dangerous stress tests automatically.

Do not make the local agent execute arbitrary commands provided by the frontend.

# 19. DATA PRIVACY

Privacy must be built into the application.

By default:
- Collect hardware information locally.
- Do not require users to create an account for basic diagnostics.
- Do not upload hardware reports automatically.
- Do not collect personal files.
- Do not scan file contents without explicit permission.
- Allow users to delete saved diagnostic history.
- Clearly communicate what information is collected.

Cloud synchronization can be optional in a future version.

